.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt FSCK_MSDOSFS 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsck_msdosfs
.Nd check and repair a FAT file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl CfnpyM
.Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks a FAT12, FAT16 or FAT32 file system, and repairs what it can.
.Xr fsck 8
runs it for
.Xr fstab 5
lines of type
.Cm msdosfs
with a pass number.
.Pp
It reads the boot sector and every copy of the FAT, and checks that each FAT
entry names a cluster of the volume, the end of a chain, a bad cluster or a free
one.
It walks the tree from the root, each file and directory claiming its chain of
clusters, finding chains that cross another or loop, that run past their file's
size or stop short of it, broken
.Ql \&.
and
.Ql \&..
entries, long-name entries without their short entry, and volume labels outside
the root.
Clusters nothing claims are lost: each lost chain is saved as
.Pa LOST.DIR/FILE Ns Ar nnnn Ns Pa .CHK ,
.Pa LOST.DIR
made if missing.
Last, the free cluster count and FAT32's FSInfo sector are corrected, and the
volume is marked clean: FAT16 and FAT32 keep a clean bit in the FAT, cleared
while the volume is mounted read-write; FAT12 has none.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl C
Skip a volume marked clean.
.It Fl f
Check a clean volume even in preen mode.
.It Fl n
Report only: open the device read-only and answer no to every repair.
.It Fl p
Preen: repair, without asking, what an interrupted write leaves (FAT copies that
differ, a chain longer or shorter than its file or ending in a free cluster, lost
clusters, stray long-name entries); stop with status 8 at anything worse.
A volume marked clean is skipped unless
.Fl f
is given, and one mounted read-write is left alone.
.It Fl y
Repair everything: truncate a chain where it crosses another, loops or leaves
the volume, remove broken entries.
.It Fl M
Accepted for compatibility; ignored.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Fl p ,
.Fl y
or
.Fl n ,
nothing is repaired.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 if the volume is consistent or was made so, 8 if inconsistencies remain (or
were found with
.Fl n ) ,
16 on a usage error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr msdosfs 5 ,
.Xr fsck 8 ,
.Xr mount_msdosfs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Nm
command appeared in
.Nx 1.2
and
.Fx 3.0 .
.Sh BUGS
A crossed chain is cut where it crosses, not copied: the later file loses its
tail.
Names are not checked against the characters FAT forbids.
